WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:01.560
(ominous music)

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.720
- [Narrator] This is Snailbrook, Texas,

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.300
a new planned community outside of Austin

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.370
that Elon Musk is building for employees

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.610
at his Tesla, SpaceX,
and Boring companies.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.730
And this is Starbase, a
rocket development site

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.780
and another new Musk city with
housing for SpaceX employees

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.630
located outside of Brownsville, Texas.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:24.180
Recent construction at both of these sites

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.630
has led to speculation that
Musk is building company towns.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.300
- We think that this
Big Brother like control

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.870
that's associated with
company towns is un-American.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.270
History shows that, that has been

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.721
a big part of American industrial history.

00:00:38.721 --> 00:00:39.554
(crowd cheering)

00:00:39.554 --> 00:00:40.387
- Hey.

00:00:40.387 --> 00:00:41.400
- [Narrator] Here's why Musk might be

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.350
looking to the company town model

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.242
for his properties in Texas.

00:00:45.242 --> 00:00:47.700
(gentle music)

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.150
- My wife and I bought this
property about 10 years ago.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.610
We originally came for the nature

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.360
and the privacy and the peacefulness.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.280
- [Narrator] This is Chap Ambrose.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.280
In 2021, Elon Musk's Boring Company

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.290
bought the 70-acre cow pasture

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.690
that sat below Ambrose's property.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.280
- I am a fan of Elon Musk.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.810
I think a lot of what he does
is really cool and inspiring.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.250
- [Narrator] Such a fan, in fact,

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:17.610
he even owns a
remote-controlled cyber truck,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.682
but Ambrose quickly soured
on his new neighbors.

00:01:20.682 --> 00:01:22.740
(truck rumbling)

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.740
- It's been a radical
change since they moved in.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.510
They really are building a shipyard

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.250
in the middle of a prairie.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.960
- [Narrator] And that's
not all they're building.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.630
As first reported in the
Wall Street Journal in March,

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:36.420
in meetings with landowners
and real estate agents,

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.970
Musk and his employees describe a vision

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.150
of a Utopia along the Colorado River.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.680
Here in Bastrop County,

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.350
approximately 45 minutes
outside of Austin,

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:50.160
SpaceX is building a 500,000
square foot facility.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.370
Across the street, Boring
is building a new warehouse.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.190
Snailbrook is already home
to some Musk employees

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:57.840
who live in modular homes.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.410
There's also a pool, an
outdoor sports area, and a gym.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:05.250
Plans suggest the site will
eventually have 110 homes

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.850
and Boring plans to convert
one into a Montessori school.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.680
As of last year, Boring employees

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.210
could apply for a home with rents

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.460
starting at about $800 a month

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:16.830
for a two or three bedroom in Snailbrook.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:20.790
The median rent in Bastrop
is about $2,200 a month.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.970
For his part, Ambrose
welcomes the economic impact

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.400
that Snailbrook's residents
will bring to the area.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.920
His primary concern is how the development

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.930
could affect the local groundwater.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.300
- If you sit out and
watch the work they do,

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.070
they're not careful.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.630
- [Narrator] Recently, Boring applied

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.640
to state environmental authorities

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.550
to discharge up to 140,000 gallons

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:46.170
of industrial wastewater a
day into the Colorado River.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:47.670
Since beginning construction,

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.160
Boring has received multiple violations

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.893
from the Texas Commission
on Environmental Quality.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.670
Ever since Musk's companies
moved in next door,

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.280
Ambrose has been
documenting the development.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.050
- I'm concerned they're gonna continue

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.460
to break those permits.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.110
I mean, they are moving so quick,

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:08.370
one week to the next it can
be a radical difference.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.480
- [Narrator] Musk tweeted that

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.490
the March Wall Street Journal article

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.830
that broke the news about
Snailbrook was false,

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:17.250
but he has not specified what
in the piece was incorrect.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.290
Furthermore, the idea that Musk

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:22.080
would create his own
town isn't far-fetched.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.610
- Sometimes there's that new neighbor

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.200
that everyone can't stop talking about,

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.000
for better or for worse.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.460
- [Narrator] In 2021,
the billionaire announced

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.320
he was building the city of Starbase,

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.530
which Musk envisions
becoming a major space port.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.200
Starbase is being built
on Boca Chica Village,

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.200
a seaside hamlet surrounded
by a wildlife refuge.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.870
Located about 25 miles outside

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.540
of the southeastern Texas
city of Brownsville.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.510
SpaceX has not officially
incorporated Starbase,

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.760
but since 2012, the aerospace company

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.370
has been buying up the
area's pre-existing homes

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.070
and turning them into employee housing.

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.710
Much like Snailbrook,
Starbase's development

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.660
attracted scrutiny from residents

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:02.970
concerned that SpaceX's expansion

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.732
will come at a steep price
to the local environment.

00:04:05.732 --> 00:04:08.931
♪ You load 16 tons and what do you get? ♪

00:04:08.931 --> 00:04:11.280
♪ Another day older and deeper in debt ♪

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.790
- [Narrator] In 1947,
country singer Merle Travis

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.060
immortalized exploitative
nature of company towns

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.590
in his song "16 tons"

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:22.578
about the life of a Kentucky coal miner.

00:04:22.578 --> 00:04:25.860
♪ I owe my soul to the company store ♪

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.810
- People tend to think of about a town

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.880
where the company owns everything.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.720
Where the company has
built all the housing,

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.040
there's a company store

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.750
and many of these coal mining towns

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.780
people were not paid in American currency.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.760
They're paid in company-issued money

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.160
that's really only good
at the company store.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.710
- [Narrator] Author, Hardy
Green, has written extensively

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.600
about the history of company towns.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.330
- There is no strict
definition of a company town.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.490
A company town, there's really

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.800
only one company that dominates.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.140
But beyond that, there's a wide range.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:01.260
Some towns are more
restrictive, more exploitative

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.500
and others are more
caring and paternalistic.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.780
- [Narrator] The more
exploitative company towns

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:09.180
like the one referred to in Travis' song

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:12.330
tended to be communities based
around a single resource.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.540
- Whole towns or extractive industry towns

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:19.410
tend to be a little bit like prison camps.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.510
- [Narrator] Like Snailbrook and Starbase,

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:24.600
many of America's oldest
and best known company towns

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:27.000
like Pullman, Illinois
and Hershey, Pennsylvania

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.160
were created by wealthy industrialists

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:32.250
who envisioned idyllic
communities for their employees.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.830
- Utopian ideals have figured prominently

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.630
in a number of company towns.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:37.860
- [Narrator] Milton Hershey built

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.860
his chocolate factory
complex in rural Pennsylvania

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.740
to attract employees to what
was then a remote location.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:45.150
Hershey constructed a town.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.400
- Workers were allowed to buy the housing.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.170
They're fairly well paid.

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:53.820
The houses come with central
heating and plumbing.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.470
- [Narrator] But Milton
Hershey's relationship

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:57.060
with his employees soured.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.850
In 1937, Hershey's workers organized

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:03.270
the company's first labor
union, and went on strike.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:06.870
That's a common theme in the
history of many company towns.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.670
Like Hershey, Pullman, Illinois

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:11.580
was a paternalistic company
town that had housing,

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.190
stores, a library and churches,

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:17.400
but Pullman like Hershey
eventually ran into trouble.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.550
In 1894, Pullman cut jobs and wages,

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:22.650
sparking a violent worker's strike.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.920
- It started off being an experiment that

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:29.580
the founders thought would be
a kind of paternalistic place,

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.320
but it didn't work out.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.370
- [Narrator] According to Green,

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.380
Musk's towns somewhat resemble

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.840
the paternalistic company towns of old.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.610
- Yeah, you could argue that Musk

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:41.160
is employing a kind of a throwback idea

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.920
of starting from scratch
in an undeveloped area.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.210
- [Narrator] An undeveloped area

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.010
that is being developed quickly

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:50.310
even as it is under the
close watch of Chap Ambrose.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:53.430
- We're not anti-growth,
we're not anti-Elon,

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.500
but we are pro-clean water.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.320
And unfortunately, those opposing forces

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.798
seem to be coming to head for some reason.

00:07:01.798 --> 00:07:03.540
(ominous music)

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:05.730
- [Narrator] Whether
Snailbrook or Starbase

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:08.520
will avoid the pitfalls
of previous company towns

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:09.870
remains to be seen.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.880
Neither have yet been incorporated,

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.000
so technically, neither
exists in a legal sense,

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.970
but if Musk does decide
to incorporate either town

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.560
that shouldn't be too difficult.

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:23.250
In Texas, as soon as a
community has 201 residents

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.323
it can petition to incorporate.

00:07:26.457 --> 00:07:29.957
(ominous music continues)

